        {
          "path": "_m/u/3/b/v/tuborg-bottle-wp/denmark-0515-have-a-beer-40137.jpg",
          "filename": "Denmark 0515 - Have a Beer! (4013775735).jpg",
          "caption": "Another bus shot....\nTurborg Bottle, 26m high, is an observation tower which originally housed Denmark’s first-ever elevator and was built for the Nordic Industry Exhibition in 1888 as a symbol of technological advancement. Used to advertise, the advent of bottled beer to the Danes. Built by the Tuborg Breweries, it originally stood close to the Copenhagen City Hall, but after the exhibition the giant bottle was moved to Hellerup. The tower also can contain the frothy liquid equivalent of 1.5 million regular beer bottles.",
          "alt": "Another bus shot....\nTurborg Bottle, 26m high, is an observation tower which originally housed Denmark’s first-ever elevator and was built for the Nordic Industry Exhibition in 1888 as a symbol of technological advancement. Used to advertise, the advent of bottled beer to the Danes. Built by the Tuborg Breweries, it originally stood close to the Copenhagen City Hall, but after the exhibition the giant bottle was moved to Hellerup. The tower also can contain the frothy liquid equivalent of 1.5 million regular beer bottles.",
